Follow-up to #88, found while factoring the Engine::Gemini endpoint seam.

#88 routed the three Gemini.pm call sites through gemini_url / gemini_model_url /
gemini_api_version / gemini_auth_query. Role::CachedContent (composed only by
Engine::Gemini) still builds its own URLs and places the credential itself:

  lib/Langertha/Role/CachedContent.pm:69   $self->url . "/v1beta/cachedContents"
  lib/Langertha/Role/CachedContent.pm:89   $self->url . "/v1beta/" . $name
  :139  POST   $url . "?key=" . $self->api_key
  :175  GET    $url . "?key=" . $self->api_key
  :210  list   query_form( key => $self->api_key )
  :276  PATCH  query_form( key => $self->api_key, updateMask => ... )
  :307  DELETE $url . "?key=" . $self->api_key

Consequence: a subclass that overrides the seam (header auth, /v1 instead of /v1beta,
another base path) gets correct chat + model-listing URLs but the cachedContents lifecycle
keeps sending ?key= against /v1beta - a half-converted shim.

Fix shape (again: only WHEN a shim is actually wanted, ADR 0016 decision 3): have the role
call the consumer's seam - $self->gemini_url("cachedContents", ...) - guarded by can(), the
way _assert_http_seam already guards url/api_key/user_agent. That drags a Gemini-named method
into a role, so the naming needs a decision (rename the seam, or `requires` it on the role).
Not done in #88 to keep that ticket a pure structural move on Engine::Gemini.

Note: cachedContents is a top-level collection, NOT under models/, so it needs gemini_url,
not gemini_model_url.
Done (worker-cachedcontent), not committed.

Chosen coupling: `requires qw( gemini_endpoint gemini_url )` on Role::CachedContent - option
(a) from the ticket. The seam methods are plain subs, installed at compile time, so they exist
when Gemini's runtime `with` runs; requires holds and fails at composition instead of at the
first HTTP call. No neutral alias: single consumer, ADR 0016 classes CachedContent as a
capability role, an indirection with one implementation would be speculative (house rule 2).

Engine::Gemini touched minimally: gemini_endpoint extracted out of gemini_url (path half of
the seam, credential-free). Needed because t/47 pins _cached_contents_url / _cached_content_url
with a \z anchor, i.e. they must stay query-free; gemini_url always appends the auth query.
gemini_url now calls gemini_endpoint, so no behaviour moved.

Role now holds only the resource paths (_cached_contents_path / _cached_content_path); all five
request sites go through gemini_url. url + api_key dropped from _assert_http_seam - the role
reads neither any more, and requiring api_key would block an ADC/mTLS consumer.

URL byte-identity verified by diffing 14 generated URLs (whole lifecycle + chat + stream +
model listing) old-vs-new with a recording UA: identical, except the paginated list, whose old
query order was randomised by Perl hash ordering (?pageSize=50&key=... vs ?key=...&pageSize=50,
varied run to run) and is now stable with the auth pair first, matching list_models_request.
pageToken percent-encoding preserved (URI round-trip kept for opaque pagination values).

New test t/48_gemini_cached_content_seam.t (23 assertions): Developer-API pin for all five
lifecycle URLs + an inline Vertex-shaped shim (other base URL, v1, projects/{p}/locations/{l}
prefix via gemini_endpoint, empty gemini_auth_query, Bearer header) proving the lifecycle
